{number: 129}
{title: This Is My Father’s World}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] This is my Father's [G7] world,
And [C] to my listening [G7] ears
All [C] nature [F] sings, and [C] round me [Am] rings
The [Dm] music [G7] of the [C] spheres.
This is my Father's [G7] world:
I [C] rest me in the [G7] thought
Of [C] rocks and [F] trees, of [C] skies and [Am] seas;
His [Dm] hand the [G7] wonders [C] wrought.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] This is my Father's [G7] world:
The [C] birds their carols [G7] raise,
The [C] morning [F] light, the [C] lily [Am] white,
De-[Dm] clare their [G7] Maker's [C] praise.
This is my Father's [G7] world:
He [C] shines in all that's [G7] fair;
In the [C] rustling [F] grass I [C] hear Him [Am] pass,
He [Dm] speaks to [G7] me every-[C] where.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] This is my Father's [G7] world:
O [C] let me ne'er for-[G7] get
That [C] though the [F] wrong seems [C] oft so [Am] strong,
God [Dm] is the [G7] Ruler [C] yet.
This is my Father's [G7] world:
Why [C] should my heart be [G7] sad?
The [C] Lord is [F] King: let the [C] heavens [Am] ring!
God [Dm] reigns; let [G7] earth be [C] glad!
{end_of_verse}
